1
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:20,039
Class,

2
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:22,719
today the topic of our essay is

3
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:23,920
"Dreams."

4
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,399
Now, before we start writing,

5
00:00:26,559 --> 00:00:28,480
I'd like to ask everyone,

6
00:00:28,719 --> 00:00:31,800
what do you want to be when you grow up?

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,560
Who would like to share?

8
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:36,600
Lin Ran, you go first.

9
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,240
I want to be a painter when I grow up.

10
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,439
And why is that?

11
00:00:41,119 --> 00:00:44,399
There are so many beautiful things in life.

12
00:00:44,799 --> 00:00:46,119
I'm afraid I'll forget them later on,

13
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:48,200
so I want to capture them with my brush.

14
00:00:49,079 --> 00:00:49,840
That's great.

15
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,920
Does anyone else want to share?

16
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:53,880
Actually, I have other things I want to do.

17
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,920
Like dressing people up beautifully.

18
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:56,719
Like what?

19
00:00:57,399 --> 00:00:58,280
Like an athlete.

20
00:00:58,560 --> 00:00:59,560
Winning gold medals in competitions.

21
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:01,920
Or doing makeup for others.

22
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,319
That's also very fun.

23
00:01:06,599 --> 00:01:07,719
Very nice, very nice.

24
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,760
And playing video games.

25
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:11,640
I really like playing games.

26
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:13,840
Actually, I like gaming the most.

27
00:01:17,359 --> 00:01:18,319
Good, good.

28
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:19,799
But, you know,

29
00:01:19,799 --> 00:01:22,879
we need to focus more on what we do.

30
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,480
Being able to do one thing well

31
00:01:24,599 --> 00:01:25,680
is already good enough.

32
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,599
Have a seat.

33
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,560
Sun Jie, your turn.

34
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,040
I want to be a scientist.

35
00:01:35,599 --> 00:01:37,000
I want to study spaceships

36
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,359
and explore the universe.

37
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:39,359
Excellent.

38
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,719
Looks like she's determined not to see us.

39
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,239
Making a mountain out of a molehill.

40
00:02:02,319 --> 00:02:03,280
Am I wrong?

41
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:03,920
I...

42
00:02:04,359 --> 00:02:04,879
Fine, okay, okay.

43
00:02:04,879 --> 00:02:05,439
Alright, alright.

44
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:10,879
Haven't you ever wondered

45
00:02:11,599 --> 00:02:12,759
why she lost control?

46
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,280
How should I know?

47
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:18,159
Last night, we all talked about our own problems,

48
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,479
but we didn't listen to hers.

49
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:24,120
Yeah, we were definitely out of line.

50
00:02:25,159 --> 00:02:26,599
But even if we want to apologize to her,

51
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,800
we still need to see her.

52
00:02:28,639 --> 00:02:29,759
Maybe

53
00:02:30,599 --> 00:02:32,240
we can start with her problem.

54
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,120
Start with her problem how?

55
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,400
We don't have a single clue.

56
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:37,800
There is a clue.

57
00:02:37,879 --> 00:02:39,280
You just didn't care enough to notice.

58
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,520
Tell us, then.

59
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,360
Last night,

60
00:02:45,919 --> 00:02:47,719
weren't you trying to swap time with her?

61
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,840
Yeah, and didn't she refuse?

62
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,360
Do you think that fits her personality?

63
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:00,960
No, it doesn't.

64
00:03:02,719 --> 00:03:03,840
She rarely refuses us.

65
00:03:16,759 --> 00:03:17,800
This morning,

66
00:03:18,479 --> 00:03:20,639
she must've had something important to do.

67
00:03:24,479 --> 00:03:25,240
Is it here?

68
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,280
This should be it.

69
00:03:30,039 --> 00:03:30,840
Teacher Lin.

70
00:03:33,319 --> 00:03:34,599
Why are you late today?

71
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:36,639
Who is this?

72
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:38,680
Probably the boss here.

73
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:39,759
Shut up!

74
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:41,840
What?

75
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,360
You're telling me to shut up?

76
00:03:43,479 --> 00:03:44,439
No, no, no.

77
00:03:44,439 --> 00:03:45,199
No, Principal.

78
00:03:45,199 --> 00:03:46,479
I wasn't talking to you.

79
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,680
I just woke up late today.

80
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:49,560
Don't let it happen again.

81
00:03:49,919 --> 00:03:50,599
Okay.

82
00:03:52,439 --> 00:03:53,240
As long as you're okay.

83
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,560
Go to your class now.

84
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,479
Listen up. From now on, around outsiders,

85
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,520
I'll do all the talking.

86
00:04:07,319 --> 00:04:08,159
I wasn't paying attention just now.

87
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,520
I accidentally took control of the body.

88
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,639
Right. We won't do it again.

89
00:04:12,599 --> 00:04:13,240
Anyway,

90
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:15,960
just keep your mouths shut.

91
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:21,519
Move.

92
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:35,639
Come on, say something.

93
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,439
Yeah, at least say a few words.

94
00:04:45,319 --> 00:04:46,560
Alright, kids.

95
00:04:47,399 --> 00:04:48,279
Today, we

96
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:49,920
aren't learning any techniques.

97
00:04:50,279 --> 00:04:51,680
We're having a pop quiz.

98
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,519
Just draw

99
00:04:54,399 --> 00:04:55,360
my face.

100
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:05,920
No laughing.

101
00:05:09,319 --> 00:05:10,000
Draw the face.

102
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:23,959
What is this supposed to be?

103
00:05:24,839 --> 00:05:25,480
Where is the person?

104
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,160
Where's this person?

105
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,639
I don't know.

106
00:05:27,959 --> 00:05:28,800
It's pretty good.

107
00:05:32,439 --> 00:05:33,759
Sweetie, you draw really well.

108
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:36,120
But I want to tell you,

109
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,519
look here.

110
00:05:37,519 --> 00:05:39,439
We can add a little blush.

111
00:05:39,439 --> 00:05:40,639
Right here on the cheekbones.

112
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:41,879
And like here, around the eyes.

113
00:05:41,879 --> 00:05:43,360
We can also add some shading.

114
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,120
Teacher!

115
00:05:46,399 --> 00:05:49,079
Why do I feel like it's a bit like... putting on makeup?

116
00:05:49,279 --> 00:05:49,839
That's right.

117
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:51,079
Putting on makeup

118
00:05:51,519 --> 00:05:53,680
is basically drawing on a person's face, right?

119
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Alright, for today's class,

120
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:58,920
we'll stop here for now.

121
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,639
But before we finish,

122
00:06:01,759 --> 00:06:03,879
I have a question for you all.

123
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,879
Does anyone know

124
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,680
what I'm going to do today?

125
00:06:09,199 --> 00:06:10,959
You're asking way too directly.

126
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,399
Yeah, even if something happened,

127
00:06:12,399 --> 00:06:13,680
the kids wouldn't necessarily know.

128
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:14,920
Draw you!

129
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:16,680
Besides that?

130
00:06:17,319 --> 00:06:18,560
Have a test!

131
00:06:19,319 --> 00:06:20,279
Let me change the question.

132
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:27,920
Did anything special happen yesterday?

133
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,480
No.

134
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,279
Yes.

135
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,639
You took me to the hospital yesterday.

136
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:36,600
The hospital?

137
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,600
Xiao Mei, let's go.

138
00:06:44,319 --> 00:06:45,319
Coming, coming!

139
00:06:53,279 --> 00:06:53,920
Xiao Mei.

140
00:06:54,319 --> 00:06:55,040
Where's Teacher Lin?

141
00:06:55,759 --> 00:06:56,399
I don't know.

142
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:58,480
Look at my drawing of Teacher Lin.

143
00:07:01,199 --> 00:07:02,240
It's really pretty.

144
00:07:04,199 --> 00:07:04,839
Yeah.

145
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:07,000
But Teacher Lin is acting a bit weird today.

146
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,360
She seems a bit mad.

147
00:07:08,519 --> 00:07:10,000
What's wrong? Did you upset her?

148
00:07:10,399 --> 00:07:11,279
I don't know.

149
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:18,120
Did you notice that?

150
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,240
I noticed.

151
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:20,639
Notice what?

152
00:07:20,879 --> 00:07:21,560
I don't know.

153
00:07:23,639 --> 00:07:26,079
This might be the problem Lin Ran faced.

154
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,800
Hello, I'd like a single-scoop ice cream.

155
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,399
Sure.

156
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,399
About me buying you ice cream today,

157
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,560
you can't tell your mom, okay?

158
00:07:37,839 --> 00:07:39,079
I'm not stupid.

159
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,360
Be good.

160
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,439
Do you guys think he and Lin Ran

161
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,920
have something going on?

162
00:07:51,279 --> 00:07:51,600
Hmm.

163
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:53,639
What makes you say that?

164
00:07:55,199 --> 00:07:57,759
A woman's intuition.

165
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,240
That actually makes some sense.

166
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,480
When Xiao Mei went to the hospital,

167
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,439
her parents definitely went too.

168
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:08,600
Maybe something happened between them then.

169
00:08:09,399 --> 00:08:10,079
Like a fight?

170
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,319
How should I know?

171
00:08:12,079 --> 00:08:13,319
No point in guessing.

172
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:36,000
I took Xiao Mei to the hospital yesterday.

173
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,480
Were you there too?

174
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,200
You don't have to do this, you know.

175
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,480
If you want to reject me,

176
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,279
you can just say it.

177
00:08:46,679 --> 00:08:47,480
Reject?

178
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:52,759
Did you ask me for something?

179
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:59,240
Did you really lose your memory?

180
00:09:01,519 --> 00:09:02,279
Dating.

181
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,639
I thought about it for a long time.

182
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:07,840
Are you willing?

183
00:09:09,639 --> 00:09:11,399
It's not a matter of wanting to or not.

184
00:09:12,559 --> 00:09:13,559
Then what is it?

185
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:18,759
My situation is a bit complicated.

186
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:22,519
I know we haven't interacted much.

187
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:24,759
We only got to know each other a bit at the training center.

188
00:09:25,639 --> 00:09:28,000
But I think liking someone is a feeling.

189
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,440
And I also secretly

190
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,240
asked your colleagues at the training center.

191
00:09:32,639 --> 00:09:34,200
You are indeed single.

192
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:37,919
You are single, right?

193
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,200
That is true.

194
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,240
But it's not...

195
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:43,879
It's not as simple as you think.

196
00:09:45,399 --> 00:09:46,399
How complicated can it be?

197
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:47,960
Let me ask you this.

198
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,120
Do you hate me?

199
00:09:49,639 --> 00:09:50,240
No.

200
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:51,360
Do you have feelings for me?

201
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:52,320
Yes.

202
00:09:52,559 --> 00:09:53,279
Then there you go.

203
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,639
Then we can totally give it a try.

204
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,039
Just consider it giving each other a chance.

205
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,879
I need to think about it.

206
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,639
I'm not brushing you off.

207
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,039
How about tomorrow morning?

208
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:11,440
I'll give you an answer.

209
00:10:13,679 --> 00:10:14,240
Okay.

210
00:10:15,639 --> 00:10:16,320
I'll wait for you.

211
00:10:17,559 --> 00:10:18,279
Yes!

212
00:10:21,519 --> 00:10:23,639
You really don't remember?

213
00:10:24,879 --> 00:10:26,279
So,

214
00:10:27,279 --> 00:10:30,519
you've been waiting for my answer all morning?

215
00:10:33,279 --> 00:10:35,399
You didn't say anything.

216
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,240
I thought you rejected me.

217
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,519
Come on, you're a grown man.

218
00:10:38,519 --> 00:10:39,720
You're giving up that easily?

219
00:10:42,279 --> 00:10:43,440
If I didn't come looking for you,

220
00:10:43,799 --> 00:10:45,159
wouldn't you have lost your chance completely?

221
00:10:47,279 --> 00:10:48,480
Are you saying

222
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:49,840
I still have a chance?

223
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,519
I didn't say that.

224
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:02,279
When did you divorce Xiao Mei's mother?

225
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:03,679
Who?

226
00:11:03,879 --> 00:11:05,720
You and Xiao Mei's mother.

227
00:11:07,639 --> 00:11:09,360
When did you get divorced?

228
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,399
Divorced?

229
00:11:11,519 --> 00:11:12,320
Yeah.

230
00:11:14,559 --> 00:11:15,200
Well...

231
00:11:16,159 --> 00:11:18,120
You're not still married, are you?

232
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:20,960
Scumbag!

233
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,039
Here, let me take over.

234
00:11:22,159 --> 00:11:23,000
Teach him a lesson!

235
00:11:24,759 --> 00:11:26,840
If you think I'd be the other woman,

236
00:11:27,279 --> 00:11:29,279
then you misjudge me.

237
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:33,759
Now I believe...

238
00:11:33,759 --> 00:11:34,360
Uncle!

239
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:37,720
I finished it. I want another one.

240
00:11:38,519 --> 00:11:39,120
No way.

241
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:40,000
You can't have any more.

242
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,360
If you eat more, your mom will scold me.

243
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:43,879
Go watch some cartoons by yourself for a bit.

244
00:11:52,919 --> 00:11:55,240
So you're her uncle.

245
00:11:56,960 --> 00:11:57,519
Yeah.

246
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,600
Xiao Mei is your student,

247
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,360
and I'm her uncle.

248
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,480
Her mom is my older sister.

249
00:12:07,559 --> 00:12:09,399
It seems we really don't know much about each other.

250
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,919
Yeah, that's what I said last time.

251
00:12:11,919 --> 00:12:13,519
I said we don't know much about each other.

252
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:16,000
That's true, that's true.

253
00:12:22,639 --> 00:12:25,200
Then how about we spend a day

254
00:12:26,039 --> 00:12:27,080
and go on a date?

255
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,240
A date?
